# NEXUS secret-scan exceptions (roadmap H1).
#
# Every line is a reviewed exception that suppresses a secret finding during
# `secretscan` / the pre-commit hook. Keep this file small, reviewed, and
# committed so exceptions stay auditable.
#
# Format (one per line):
#   <path-glob>[:<kind>]    # why this is not a real secret
#
# * `path-glob` is matched against the reported file path (fnmatch); a trailing
#   "/" matches everything under that directory.
# * `kind` (optional) restricts the exception to one signature, e.g. `openai_key`.
# * the `# reason` is REQUIRED - entries without a reason are ignored (and
#   reported as invalid), so an unreviewed exception can never suppress a secret.
#
# Signature kinds (see lib/selfscan.py): discord_webhook, telegram_bot_token,
# openai_key, github_token, aws_access_key, google_api_key, slack_token,
# private_key, generic_bearer.
#
# Examples (kept commented so the default file suppresses nothing):
#   docs/examples/*            # documentation placeholders only
#   tools/fixtures/keys.txt:aws_access_key   # synthetic AWS key in a test fixture
